+## Managed native environments (schema 3)
+
+Build with `cargo build --locked --release -p obscura-cli --features render --bin obscura`.
+The macOS graphics backend requires the system OpenGL framework and an available CGL context.
+
+```bash
+obscura --environment-config /profiles/A/config.json serve \
+  --host 127.0.0.1 --port 0 --workers 1 \
+  --storage-dir /profiles/A/data --ready-file /profiles/A/ready.json
+```
+
+The configuration file and data directory are independent locations. The host supplies all
+resolved fields; the runtime does not regenerate identity defaults. The native
+`Environment.getInfo` CDP method reports schema, id, revision, the SHA-256 of the exact
+loaded file bytes, source version, validated assets, and initialized backend capabilities.
+Configuration, font/backend validation and storage restoration precede readiness.
+Unknown fields, unapplied overrides, incompatible revisions and missing assets fail startup.
+Manager metadata `created_at` is an optional string, and migration metadata
+`previous_environment_sha256` is an optional string binding the previous raw-file digest.
+Both remain part of the exact input bytes hashed in the native receipt; they are not
+removed or recanonicalized. Other unknown root fields still fail deserialization.
+Resolved-input and render-configuration object digests explicitly sort keys recursively
+before compact UTF-8 serialization, regardless of serde_json's `preserve_order` feature.
+Their canonical JSON digests exclude a trailing newline; the environment receipt instead
+hashes every byte of the original file, including its actual newline and metadata.
+An output-affecting change requires the previous raw environment digest and a strictly newer
+revision. Byte-identical asset/runtime relocation, data path and manager name/mode changes may
+retain the revision; the receipt still binds the newly loaded raw file bytes. The manager must
+preserve a compatible stopped storage snapshot before semantic migration or rollback.
+
+`asset_paths.fonts` lists explicit absolute font files. The font asset digest is the SHA-256
+of the canonical sorted unique list of file SHA-256 strings, independent of deployment paths.
+CJK requires a real, versioned CJK font in that list.
+`resolved.fonts` optionally restricts actual font families. CSS and Canvas use the same
+font assets and cosmic-text/Swash rasterization. Canvas geometry uses tiny-skia; WebGL
+executes through CGL/OpenGL rather than synthetic renderer identifiers. Driver and
+subset limitations are included in the native capability details.
+WebGL resource creators return concrete resource-owning `WebGL*` instances with
+private native identity, context and lifetime records. Liveness, errors, shader
+compilation/logs and rendering query the actual driver; deleted/foreign/forged
+wrappers cannot gain resource ownership. No prototype or function-source relabeling
+is used to manufacture brands.
+Native input/textarea values, placeholders, password-mask bullets and select labels use
+the document's cosmic-text/Swash engine, CSS font attributes and control content clips.
+Empty live values remain empty rather than restoring HTML defaults. Control column widths,
+button labels and selected-font line metrics use actual shaped advances, not character-count
+or embedded bitmap-font estimates. Password text is masked before shaping.
+Child-frame screenshots recursively render the same loaded native child DOMs and their
+resource caches, using the existing surface hook and actual content-box dimensions,
+scroll state, transforms, clipping and stacking. No second browser or execution DOM is
+used. Frame metadata and default execution contexts identify those actual native realms.
+Content/padding/border/margin quads come from retained layout geometry, not synthetic sizes.
+Surface destinations and rounded clips use the renderer's actual raster scale once;
+ancestor masks retain their device-pixel basis. Native child surfaces are borrowed
+as premultiplied RGBA, preserving transparent backgrounds and authored alpha without
+a copy/demultiply/premultiply cycle. Canvas straight-RGBA inputs retain their existing path.
+
+CSS interaction selectors consume the authoritative DOM's focused, active and hovered
+node IDs. The shared renderer exposes `set_focused`, `set_active`, `set_hovered` and
+`set_focus_visible`; read-only projections must supply actual runtime state, not CSS
+attributes. Focus-within, active and hover follow ordinary and shadow-host ancestry.
+Disconnecting a subtree clears its input states. Native focus/blur and pointer input
+update these states and invalidate cached style/layout. Focus-visible follows native
+keyboard versus pointer modality, retaining visibility for text-input/editable controls;
+it is not an alias for focus or an unconditional renderer effect.
+
+Generator `native-3.2` materializes `resolved.gl_backend`: `cgl-default`,
+`cgl-accelerated`, or `cgl-generic-float`. It participates in the render configuration
+digest and selects real CGL pixel-format constraints, with no fallback when unavailable.
+The driver vendor/renderer/version are queried from the selected context. Different
+real backends do not guarantee different pixels for a given shader; equal samples remain
+equal observations, and the full differentiation gate remains outstanding.
+
+Managed mode accepts only deny permissions and rejects stealth/UA/font-directory overrides.
+Proxy secrets use `network.proxy_ref: \"env:VARIABLE\"`; the launcher places the resolved
+value in `OBSCURA_PROXY`. Only HTTP, HTTPS and remote-DNS `socks5h` proxies are accepted.
+The explicit proxy applies to navigation, resources and Worker fetch; transport errors
+never retry directly, and inherited system/no-proxy bypass settings are disabled.
+Absence of UDP/WebRTC transport is not evidence of complete network-leak coverage.
+
+Dedicated Worker `Request.cache` supports `default` and `no-store`, including
+inheritance and explicit overrides. The shared raw fetch transport has no HTTP
+response cache; no-store requests always reach it and carry a no-store directive
+when the caller supplied none. Native policy is preserved over redirect hops,
+without turning the transport-generated directive into an author CORS header.
+Other cache modes, non-follow redirects and non-default referrer policies remain
+explicitly unsupported rather than silently ignored.
+
+Cookie and LocalStorage mutations and IndexedDB commits use synced atomic files.
+Only acknowledged IndexedDB transactions enter the durable snapshot; live connections
+and unfinished transactions are not restored. A durable Cookie/LocalStorage I/O failure
+terminates the runtime rather than leaving uncommitted values visible to other clients.
+SessionStorage remains tab-scoped. Clear the entire data directory to reset native stores.
+The new backend sources are unverified until the integration owner runs compilation and
+the independent behavioral/identity/GUI matrix; capability implementation is not acceptance.
+
+CDP remote objects are rooted only in native V8 storage, keyed by opaque IDs and
+their actual realm/document generation. Page globals cannot inspect or replace the
+registry. `Runtime.callFunctionOn`, object arguments, `Runtime.getProperties`,
+console objects and DOM resolution share these original roots; property enumeration
+does not invoke author getters. `Runtime.releaseObject` drops its native root.
+Navigation, detached frame ownership and runtime replacement invalidate old IDs
+with `stale_reference`; no saved expression is replayed to reconstruct a handle.
+`Page.bringToFront` and `Target.activateTarget` select an existing live target in
+the session registry. They update native foreground focus/visibility state and
+deliver visibility/window focus events without replacing contexts, pages, heaps
+or retained handles. New/resumed documents inherit the page's actual activation
+state before author scripts execute. Explicit runtime destruction still invalidates
+its original roots; callers must acquire a new observation after that destruction.
+
+Locale/resolved identity is owned by native state and cached only inside the private
+bootstrap closure through a host-retained closure bridge; Deno's engine core remains
+frozen and unmodified. Focused-element state is also closure private. The runtime
+neither creates nor reads public environment/language/focus storage
+markers, and page-created properties with the obsolete names cannot alter these states.
+Getter naming and function-source presentation are not changed to impersonate another engine.
+
+The owning manager may launch with `ANTI_TRACE_PARENT_EOF=1` and an owned stdin pipe.
+The native server watches EOF on that pipe, stops page/Worker activity through its
+normal shutdown path, drains connections and flushes durable stores. It monitors no
+PID and launches no watchdog process. Standalone behavior is unchanged without the
+flag. Parent ownership loss during startup prevents readiness; shutdown removes the
+owned readiness file. The manager must preserve or reconcile profile-lock ownership
+through this asynchronous native drain before allowing another writer or export.
